    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1ec1326f_3d061045",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_prl_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 751,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-08T17:30:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I absolutely don\u0027t want us to get into PE locked scenarios.  That makes the port by and large unusable until unplug.  \n\nMy current thought for dealing with discard scenarios is to create a shared parent states can use for sending.  It would deal with the sender response timer, and checking for and redirecting on message discard.  That way we could also address inconsistencies we\u0027ve had with when the sender response timer starts, and it would reduce redundant timer code.\n\nIf we like the shared parent route, we could also include an error case for eventual giving up and resetting of the PRL layer?  Ideally, I\u0027d like to get all the bugs out of the PRL.  However  we should probably be thinking defensively about our states.",
      "parentUuid": "dcb9e1a2_31baf848",
